<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samsung wins $30 mln Indian order.</title>
<headline>Samsung wins $30 mln Indian order.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Samsung Engineering Co Ltd said on Tuesday it has won a $30 million petrochemical plant expansion order from Indian Petrochemical Corp Ltd.</p>
<p>Samsung said in a statement the expansion would boost the Indian firm's polyethylene output to 140,000 tonnes a year from current 80,000 tonnes a year.</p>
<p>The construction in Nagothane, 120 km south of Bombay, is scheduled to be completed by May 1998.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
